#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091972 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "2737e6bc-5372-50a0-bf2f-59a91f571a57" :question/math-academy-id "e-4520" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/add80202102548e61880979bc0379e0bc65f9ef7fa37173f9035410661e2b75e.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=3, y=0, z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=3+0+(-2)=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "d32f2604-fc3f-5e80-8085-483e6fd9a3ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-4521" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z=0 \\\\ z+4y-5=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/97d3c148b792d9db50bc81b8c12f1574f284746cb37b12d99a8881853bf5ea13.png)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/e93ae11a2b2d1538c4ad97bba6d92e8e17fe14c8778898365ffeda9c5d1bacee.png)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/c2492650916d7a880ea52322edb41b8127b4c31bcff0620cec3cf4e37fa7928f.png)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/dd70742ae3c6613f78305edc718b10568269b49be611643059a1e6121828f404.png)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/id #uuid "06a50eb4-4976-55fd-aa44-6509b27eccb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4604" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d},$ where $A$ and $B$ are $10 \\times 10$ non-singular matrices, while $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ are $10 \\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $\\mathbf{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse $B^{−1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d}$ by $B^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{10}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3913b813-19e1-5838-a7ce-25c5f75b98b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287649} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7fbde2-1a21-5fb1-8d83-65e0637b0829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-15,y=-10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287650} {:answer/id #uuid "d49ea752-b50e-5647-ba94-f4bf5951285c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287651} {:answer/id #uuid "42da5cbf-1dcc-5f8e-aff0-1ee1c79574da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-30,y=-20,z=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287652} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdb890a-69a1-5c8a-b553-5afded12115b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49ea752-b50e-5647-ba94-f4bf5951285c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287651} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed131fa2-13cf-592a-be0c-f93fee5f0963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e436b484-45cd-5959-9069-2880512ec233" :question/math-academy-id "q-10074" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z=-1-x \\\\ 4y=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z=0 \\\\ x+6z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "455280a6-f859-5054-803b-696ef3129529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331137} {:answer/id #uuid "d84f689a-134f-5407-b5f7-e046f6e72b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331138} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0c1bfc-c0b0-5476-9eff-a10057ad340a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331139} {:answer/id #uuid "49684f5f-864b-59c5-b876-5b3a8697f322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=49,z=58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331140} {:answer/id #uuid "ac85153a-3e2f-5e94-8d8d-4602905ebb9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac85153a-3e2f-5e94-8d8d-4602905ebb9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331141} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1033273-5d4f-5a9d-b005-946c4dd7384e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f56f052-82ef-5f6f-b9cb-411952681c67" :question/math-academy-id "q-10076" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40398599-c736-5231-83f6-dd91cf084a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287656} {:answer/id #uuid "040386b6-5143-5e39-a9e4-c69c7af3cada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287657} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b433aa-17d2-5e91-a08f-3477affa21f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287658} {:answer/id #uuid "b996bbe6-77e2-52b4-a15a-6bcb715fd96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287659} {:answer/id #uuid "9330039e-54ee-52a6-9da7-c7c1b7494f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40398599-c736-5231-83f6-dd91cf084a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287656} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e58b42b-ea48-5337-bb06-7cf540036ffb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "528b601b-5416-5158-83e1-ea8ffb44a5a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-104536" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2z=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z=2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8f212da-c62b-5b55-8dfe-f1bd1c478789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,y=-11,z=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287663} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2060ec-2e80-5939-93e4-13de7ea9dbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287664} {:answer/id #uuid "acfb8a8b-781e-5d0f-b596-bb531721e814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6,y=-3,z=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287665} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf8785b-6265-5ef0-83d0-7ea910f09768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=6,z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287666} {:answer/id #uuid "f4274771-6965-5e28-85ca-7aed5b6b1f78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11,y=6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd2060ec-2e80-5939-93e4-13de7ea9dbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287664} :answer-field/id #uuid "789a32d6-dcb0-5fd8-b255-8b4bfb37e483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf9ff59f-8ec8-569a-88c2-1ac3dd73e105" :question/math-academy-id "q-104541" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x=2 \\\\ -3z+y=3 \\\\ 2x+y=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ y-3z=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93332e7a-22dc-586a-aa99-51e6084817fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284861} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf19437-06f3-5ea2-9f83-78e1cabbc712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93332e7a-22dc-586a-aa99-51e6084817fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284861} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b9a1ffe-e77f-5ccb-9605-6219c28cdf38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16829971-5742-5fdd-be3c-ba81e527b5db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16829971-5742-5fdd-be3c-ba81e527b5db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284863} :answer-field/id #uuid "631d66aa-0440-5de3-bc37-8981c7fb0a9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e64051-2d06-5f61-9634-020fe9ceaeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29e64051-2d06-5f61-9634-020fe9ceaeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284865} :answer-field/id #uuid "33bb1b68-7b77-5cb0-940f-c98a7d0ea2a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "15fa7367-7a5a-51c5-9948-2a491219ff01" :question/math-academy-id "q-275781" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z=-1 \\\\ x-y+3z=2 \\\\ -2x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, and the inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe solution of the system of equations is \n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}, \n$\\,z=$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is \n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=0,\\,z=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "716d1d1a-decc-5153-a5ca-c4bb3512cafb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284868} {:answer/id #uuid "bc761467-a3f5-54a8-83fe-e813e7574317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc761467-a3f5-54a8-83fe-e813e7574317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284869} :answer-field/id #uuid "67debf65-e6b8-50eb-a982-2a4084d044d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d432c89-df76-51ba-adc2-3657d2b6b737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d432c89-df76-51ba-adc2-3657d2b6b737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284871} :answer-field/id #uuid "39d6b377-ea9f-5025-a00c-bcac1c32bf93" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "047b7868-3069-5421-8c42-88cbce8eecae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "047b7868-3069-5421-8c42-88cbce8eecae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284873} :answer-field/id #uuid "1694a284-2e0c-57d5-be06-d1408ca50c74" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a39e36b1-acfe-5c9b-80de-88271f2bea5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275787" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+z=4x+y+2 \\\\ x+y=2z+2 \\\\ y=x-y+z+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x-y+z=2 \\\\ x+y-2z=2 \\\\ -x+2y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1+4)+(-1-2)+(2+1) \\\\  & =-9-3+3 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29842345-b6c2-5d6d-9d82-89a73f9b97e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331145} {:answer/id #uuid "356ed408-1e33-568a-bd26-e3307d2b9b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331146} {:answer/id #uuid "c74ce52f-ebd5-5b5a-8ff2-96579f6a2943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331147} {:answer/id #uuid "73afc0ce-73e9-5fc7-8fbe-f9ac34f81ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331148} {:answer/id #uuid "864583e4-523f-5dfa-880c-aec63263656e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "864583e4-523f-5dfa-880c-aec63263656e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331149} :answer-field/id #uuid "d49f56c9-7e65-583a-b934-0a287de9762e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db6060ad-8c77-548e-9bad-ddb7a1172d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-78421" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=1 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-1,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-1)+(-2)=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7d6b37b-20a4-5dae-9714-7ccadee39dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ and $D^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091020} {:answer/id #uuid "da87e365-82b4-5b06-b200-fbccc58ed546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ and $D$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091021} {:answer/id #uuid "db19c443-a1fc-5b8b-bebd-6028e50cf51a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ and $I_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091022} {:answer/id #uuid "594c9f9a-8850-560a-9bf6-5ccbca1af66c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D^{-1}$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091023} {:answer/id #uuid "773b5340-5235-53ae-8b22-5005d3594900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$I_{3}$ and $D^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "594c9f9a-8850-560a-9bf6-5ccbca1af66c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D^{-1}$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091023} :answer-field/id #uuid "405e54ce-2163-5b71-b891-698847c6dda9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15bdd24c-e192-58dc-b8c4-b4c9d91ba43f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78442" :question/problem "Consider a system of $3$ linear equations in $3$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,y=w.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $y$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $w$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w \\\\  & ={D}^{-1}\\,w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,y=w$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,y & ={D}^{-1}w \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w \\\\ y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $y.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9535c375-2d54-5e41-a8f0-e3d677a695ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331152} {:answer/id #uuid "78413cf9-4770-5672-a06b-5c736541e297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331153} {:answer/id #uuid "125c1985-9152-5da8-abc1-0fa65030f129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331154} {:answer/id #uuid "442dac3f-64fb-54c6-b5d4-53c435ee3c63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331155} {:answer/id #uuid "cea4aaeb-7ba5-5cc5-b409-5efa13136c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "125c1985-9152-5da8-abc1-0fa65030f129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331154} :answer-field/id #uuid "6036be45-3f7b-5236-9670-640a998a7124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b5a6d2e-84ca-5b1b-8229-e89b616a1853" :question/math-academy-id "q-78551" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ 3x+2y-z=1 \\\\ x-4y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-2,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aa84d7d-1757-5dea-8820-f54c350e31d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331159} {:answer/id #uuid "7552d8e9-5a32-5505-aa29-6312c454d7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331160} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fabc54-cb32-5fe2-8133-9a3dade1fbe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331161} {:answer/id #uuid "17c06854-3e2a-5643-9ab9-adfc84f159f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331162} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2acb76-b360-5d36-8279-07de89647b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7552d8e9-5a32-5505-aa29-6312c454d7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331160} :answer-field/id #uuid "473d2ff0-b888-5fba-b140-c20e73e280c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1c000e5-dd9a-5906-a229-6843cfbdf8cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-78554" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z=0 \\\\ x+3y+z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y-z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $\\frac{yz}{x}?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=-1,z=3.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{yz}{x}=\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3}{-1}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f943ff-0c2a-5b06-8bef-42ab98671fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091050} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f36725-cb69-5eb2-8330-0b8f600b011d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091051} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c1a2fe-fb8d-5338-a8d0-e73336e6ce9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091052} {:answer/id #uuid "00a602e6-98bf-544e-a82e-58cca7fcff8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091053} {:answer/id #uuid "0ad8560c-81b8-5288-8ccd-f8a29d4510cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f36725-cb69-5eb2-8330-0b8f600b011d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091051} :answer-field/id #uuid "d13343dd-0fe9-59b1-847f-d9dc33737c2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35f6dc89-f4a6-5953-a50e-5f17ce4b6254" :question/math-academy-id "q-78557" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=2 \\\\ x-2y-5z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y+2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=5,y=3,z=0.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=5+3+0=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a518b603-68cf-5081-a006-bebec39c0ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284904} {:answer/id #uuid "c9aeeb5d-fde3-5d0e-8807-a207ea073ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284905} {:answer/id #uuid "be38daad-9f0f-52d8-99b5-268b10c565c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284906} {:answer/id #uuid "d679bd28-9dfc-59b9-80cd-cc4e4da62788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $D$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284907} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff1d0cd-155c-5e4a-bb8b-1696cfc9d17a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ and $q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a518b603-68cf-5081-a006-bebec39c0ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284904} :answer-field/id #uuid "509dc752-679a-5a25-b0a5-555c3f377233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ecf8e0a5-c1dd-5243-9116-de59a516e7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-78561" :question/problem "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,t=q.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $t$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $q$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\, \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,t=q$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb7f731e-bcdb-5099-ba3c-b6da5b2d0b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331166} {:answer/id #uuid "5790b096-f0ce-5afc-bfb8-66f8573cd6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=d\\,{A}^{-1}B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331167} {:answer/id #uuid "10777031-1f86-5194-b6f8-92deeb7e7339" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=B\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331168} {:answer/id #uuid "3496926d-e3dc-5f49-95f0-f444cd83a071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=B{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331169} {:answer/id #uuid "93c4d244-6e10-5249-b01a-27a323f6d7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}\\,d\\,B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7f731e-bcdb-5099-ba3c-b6da5b2d0b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331166} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d53b8af-4f7a-5df4-bee8-6dfc934aacc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f46dcea5-1f8c-5ca6-bcf8-024327ec2e37" :question/math-academy-id "q-78563" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $A\\,x=B\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A\\,x=B\\,d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,x & =B\\,d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\,x & ={A}^{-1}B\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}B\\,d \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}B\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91a107e-9f80-5278-a498-ecf78c338881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=AB\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331173} {:answer/id #uuid "7f791699-f330-5e27-be89-31bb2628e35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331174} {:answer/id #uuid "24c2ebf6-4fc7-546c-bf5f-a9da60c5f3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=d\\,AB" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331175} {:answer/id #uuid "cc8d39a5-78b9-5d1e-95d5-fe61d3ed1f5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331176} {:answer/id #uuid "366f4140-c8bb-5bb1-afee-426a78f9bc2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f791699-f330-5e27-be89-31bb2628e35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331174} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3757bf-b37c-5fcf-a6c9-45c2b4ba907e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9038fac-5f35-5ebb-bf51-e55eda35beaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-78566" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $3\\times 3$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x=d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{3}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x=A\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ x & =BA\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "159ea08a-8ea8-5765-b005-b2a6ddd80e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284918} {:answer/id #uuid "0b6eff45-2b53-5342-b6be-ad7f718df3f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284919} {:answer/id #uuid "0db913f7-47b3-5c1e-8133-1d15c0b640c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284920} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bd2c5c-914a-5ff4-9132-4f885d7db5d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284921} {:answer/id #uuid "e9410667-0a4e-5a73-9c2a-9fc6881ff150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8bd2c5c-914a-5ff4-9132-4f885d7db5d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284921} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc88e52-3b62-5dd4-929b-309a88df9ce1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e6242987-b8d2-5395-bc4d-b5736a798e19" :question/math-academy-id "q-78571" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $A\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\,x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{2}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
